<!doctype html>
<!--
  The test door.

  Forty-three gardeners, one per language the site knows, so that what a page
  looks like to a reader of Macedonian can be looked at rather than imagined.
  Pick one and the garden is drawn in that language, with a bar across the top
  saying which one you are standing in.

  **There are no accounts here.** `Server/` is static files and this app is
  built on nothing reaching an origin. A tester is a name and a language kept in
  this browser, the word below is a latch rather than a lock, and
  `assets/js/testers.js` says so at length at the top of the file. The roster
  protects nothing: every name on it is invented and every plant behind it is
  invented, which the garden already says on its own screen.

  Static, like `/s` and `/g`: no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party
  anything.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden — testers</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Reading the garden in somebody else's language." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <!-- Not a page for anybody but whoever is building this. -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page" id="page">
      <!--
        The bar. On every page of the site, and the only way between any two of
        them that is not a link somebody happened to put in a paragraph.
        `site.css` §The bar says why it is the masthead with two things added
        rather than a header of its own.
      -->
      <header class="masthead bar">
        <span class="bar__home">
          <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
          <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
        </span>
        <!--
          The ways on from here, as glyphs rather than words, so they read the
          same in every language: the garden (the app's own Garden mark,
          `GardenGlyph` in Chrome.swift), what the names mean (an open book,
          the app's `MeaningsGlyph`), and the language. Each glyph's words
          are its name and tooltip, written from the catalogue by the page's
          script. See site.css §The bar's glyphs.
        -->
        <span class="bar__ways">
          <a class="bar-glyph" href="/garden" aria-label="The garden" title="The garden"><svg class="bar-glyph__mark" viewBox="0 0 15 15" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M 4.674 4.059 C 3.796 1.407, 6.716 1.407, 5.838 4.059 C 8.089 2.405, 8.991 5.181, 6.198 5.166 C 8.467 6.795, 6.105 8.512, 5.256 5.850 C 4.407 8.512, 2.045 6.795, 4.314 5.166 C 1.521 5.181, 2.423 2.405, 4.674 4.059 Z M 5.784 14.100 C 5.652 10.932, 5.124 9.612, 5.256 7.500 M 10.140 14.100 C 9.678 10.932, 9.150 8.556, 8.622 6.180 M 10.140 14.100 C 10.338 10.404, 10.470 6.972, 10.338 3.540 M 10.140 14.100 C 10.800 10.932, 11.658 8.820, 12.318 6.972 M 4.200 14.100 L 11.328 14.100" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg></a>
          <a class="bar-glyph" href="/meanings" aria-label="What the names mean" title="What the names mean"><svg class="bar-glyph__mark" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 5.2C8.2 3.9 5.4 3.5 2.75 3.9V15.4C5.4 15 8.2 15.4 10 16.7C11.8 15.4 14.6 15 17.25 15.4V3.9C14.6 3.5 11.8 3.9 10 5.2ZM10 5.2V16.7" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg></a>
        </span>
      </header>

      <!--
        This whole page is written in English and stays in English. It is the
        one screen that must not be in the language being tested, or it stops
        being readable at exactly the moment it is needed. It is never
        commissioned; see docs/LANGUAGES.md for what the site does
        commission and why the list is defended.
      -->
      <h1 class="heading">Testers</h1>

      <p class="body">
        One gardener per language, for looking at the garden from where a reader
        of it stands. Picking one draws every label, every passage and the whole
        page in that language until you leave.
      </p>

      <!-- 1. The latch. -->
      <form class="door" id="door">
        <label class="label" for="word">Word</label>
        <input
          class="door__field"
          id="word"
          name="word"
          type="password"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocapitalize="none"
          spellcheck="false"
        />
        <button class="quiet-button" type="submit">Open</button>
        <p class="body quiet" id="door-note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>

      <!-- 2. The roster. -->
      <section class="roster" id="roster" hidden aria-label="Testers">
        <label class="label" for="filter">Find</label>
        <input
          class="door__field"
          id="filter"
          type="search"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocapitalize="none"
          spellcheck="false"
          placeholder="Danish, da, Gartner"
        />
        <ul class="roster__list" id="roster-list"></ul>
      </section>

      <p class="notice body">
        Every plant in the garden is invented, and so is everybody on this list.
        Nothing here is stored anywhere but in this browser.
      </p>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/door.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
